{"name":"Delaware Blue Hen","hex":"#76a09e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"hen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female chicken (Gallus gallus), especially a sexually mature one kept for her eggs.","A female of other bird species, particularly a sexually mature female fowl."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Synonym of mother-hen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Delaware Blue Hen","blocks":[{"text":"The Delaware Blue Hen or Blue Hen of Delaware is a blue strain of American gamecock. Under the name Blue Hen Chicken it is the official bird of the State of Delaware. It is the emblem or mascot of several institutions in the state, among them the sports teams of the University of Delaware."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Delaware_Blue_rooster.png/330px-Delaware_Blue_rooster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delaware_Blue_Hen"},{"title":"Delaware","blocks":[{"text":"Delaware is a state in the Mid-Atlantic and South Atlantic regions of the United States. It borders Maryland to its south and west, Pennsylvania to its north, New Jersey to its northeast, and the Atlantic Ocean to its east. The state's name derives from the adjacent Delaware Bay, which in turn was named after Thomas West, 3rd Baron De La Warr, an English nobleman and the Colony of Virginia's first colonial-era governor."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Flag_of_Delaware.svg/330px-Flag_of_Delaware.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delaware"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/1999_DE_Proof.png/500px-1999_DE_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/1999_DE_Proof.png/500px-1999_DE_Proof.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1999_DE_Proof.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Recto_Delaware_2_shillings_6_pence_1777_urn-3_HBS.Baker.AC_1085935.jpeg/500px-Recto_Delaware_2_shillings_6_pence_1777_urn-3_HBS.Baker.AC_1085935.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Recto_Delaware_2_shillings_6_pence_1777_urn-3_HBS.Baker.AC_1085935.jpeg/1280px-Recto_Delaware_2_shillings_6_pence_1777